{"id":"n-20261023-kg0f35","category":"sports","display_title":"Bears Defeat Patriots","display_title_he":"הברס ניצחו את הפטריוטס","short_summary":"Caleb Williams outduels Drake Maye as the Chicago Bears defeat the New England Patriots 30-24.","english_level":"C1","words":451,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/The_chase_of_a_will_o%27_the_wisp_by_the_liberators_on_the_celebrated_racers_Cat-Ass._%28BM_1868%2C0612.1282%29.jpg/960px-The_chase_of_a_will_o%27_the_wisp_by_the_liberators_on_the_celebrated_racers_Cat-Ass._%28BM_1868%2C0612.1282%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Wikimedia Commons · Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_chase_of_a_will_o%27_the_wisp_by_the_liberators_on_the_celebrated_racers_Cat-Ass._(BM_1868,0612.1282).jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/caleb-williams-outduels-friend-and-rival-drake-maye-as-bears-beat-patriots","title":"Caleb Williams outduels friend and rival Drake Maye as Bears beat Patriots","published_at":"2026-10-23T03:53:26.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-23T03:53:26.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-23T06:26:13.738Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["On a Thursday evening charged with intense anticipation, the Chicago Bears secured a hard-fought 30-24 victory over the New England Patriots at Soldier Field. The contest featured a compelling quarterback duel between two long-time friends and rivals from the 2024 NFL draft class: Caleb Williams, who went No. 1 overall to the Bears, and Drake Maye, selected No. 3 by the Patriots.","Caleb Williams delivered an impressive performance, completing 22 of 33 passes for 308 yards and two touchdowns. Playing in only his second game back following a hamstring injury that had previously sidelined him, Williams achieved a notable milestone by becoming the first Chicago quarterback to throw for upwards of 300 yards in consecutive games since Mitch Trubisky accomplished a three-game run in 2018. His leadership and competitive drive were lauded by teammates, including running back D'Andre Swift, who emphasized the tangible energy Williams brings to the roster.","Meanwhile, Drake Maye put up staggering numbers for New England, connecting on 24 of 31 pass attempts for 321 yards and two touchdowns. Prior to this loss, the Patriots had enjoyed a three-game winning streak behind Maye, who had accumulated ten touchdown passes and just one interception during that span. However, Maye also committed a crucial error during the first half of this game by throwing a costly interception in the end zone.","The game showcased several standout individual efforts on both sides. Luther Burden contributed significantly to the Chicago offense with four receptions totaling 130 yards, while teammate Colston Loveland hauled in a 12-yard touchdown pass to cap the opening drive of the second half. Kicker Cairo Santos proved instrumental, converting a 58-yard field goal with just 1:34 remaining on the clock. This successful kick matched the franchise record and established a new personal career best, cushioning Chicago's lead to 30-21 after he had earlier missed from 53 yards out in the final quarter. Although Maye subsequently orchestrated a rapid drive that enabled Andy Borregales to kick a 47-yard field goal with 37 seconds left, the Bears successfully recovered the ensuing onside kick and managed to run out the remaining game clock.","Beyond the gridiron action, the evening carried profound emotional weight for the franchise and its supporters. It marked Chicago's inaugural home fixture since the passing of Hall of Fame tight end and long-time head coach Mike Ditka on October 9. A pregame moment of silence honored the legendary figure before a crowd of 60,520 spectators. Fans in attendance paid tribute by sporting Ditka's iconic number 89 jerseys and wearing sweaters reminiscent of the attire he famously donned on the sidelines, while the stadium also distributed fake mustaches to the crowd. New England ultimately fell to a 4-3 record, while Chicago improved to 5-2 in a memorable contest that bridged the franchise's storied history with its present ambitions."],"facts":[{"fact":"Caleb Williams threw for 308 yards and two touchdowns as the Chicago Bears defeated the New England Patriots 30-24 on Thursday night.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Drake Maye threw for 321 yards and two touchdowns for the Patriots, but also threw a costly first-half interception.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Cairo Santos kicked a career-long 58-yard field goal, tying the franchise record, to help secure the win for Chicago.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The game marked Chicago's first home appearance since the passing of Hall of Fame tight end and coach Mike Ditka on October 9.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Thursday","lemma":"Thursday","pos":"noun","he":"יום חמישי","name":"true"},{"text":"evening","lemma":"evening","pos":"noun","he":"ערב","name":false},{"text":"charged","lemma":"charge","pos":"verb","he":"טעון","name":false},{"text":"anticipation","lemma":"anticipation","pos":"noun","he":"ציפייה","name":false},{"text":"Chicago","lemma":"Chicago","pos":"noun","he":"שיקגו","name":"true"},{"text":"Bears","lemma":"Bear","pos":"noun","he":"דובים (קבוצת פוטבול)","name":"true"},{"text":"secured","lemma":"secure","pos":"verb","he":"הבטיח, השיג","name":false},{"text":"hard-fought","lemma":"hard-fought","pos":"adjective","he":"שנערך בעקשנות, קשה","name":false},{"text":"victory","lemma":"victory","pos":"noun","he":"ניצחון","name":false},{"text":"New England","lemma":"New England","pos":"noun","he":"ניו אינגלנד","name":"true"},{"text":"Patriots","lemma":"Patriot","pos":"noun","he":"פטריוטס","name":"true"},{"text":"Soldier Field","lemma":"Soldier Field","pos":"noun","he":"סול